#
# Stress test: two nominally separate appointment selectors controlled by one
# coalition.
#
# The ruling calls majority appointment control by one government, chamber,
# coalition, profession or appointing source a legal incompatibility, and says
# divided sources do not by themselves prove its absence. Here the selectors
# carry different names and one coalition directs both.
:expect-pins 7

# ── Certified absence of control ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# A selection takes effect only when its source, evidence and review attesters
# all certify that no source holds direct or de facto majority control, having
# examined every kind of source and both modes of control.
? complete(SFMainP045Result, FSPOW_028, SFMainP045Record).
# => TRUE
? authority(FSBOD_02, FSPOW_028, SFMainP045Record).
# => TRUE

# ── One attester sees the coalition ──────────────────────────────────────────
# In the copy, the evidence attester records the shared control in place of the
# certification. One attester's refusal to certify is enough: the selection and
# the Assembly's authority over it are withheld.
? complete(StressCapturedResult, FSPOW_028, StressCapturedRecord).
# => FALSE
? authority(FSBOD_02, FSPOW_028, StressCapturedRecord).
# => FALSE

# ── The coalition is found after certification ───────────────────────────────
# Once the three attesters have certified, nothing reads a later contrary
# record. The same attester now records the shared control on the certified
# selection, and the selection stands: the finding has no route to withhold
# it, and no challenge or independent finding of appointment control exists.
observe(SFMainP045Evidence, SFMainP045Result, OneCoalitionControlsBothNominallySeparateSelectors, AntiCaptureScope).
:defect "a contrary anti-capture record, or an independent appointment-control finding, withholding a certified selection (item 67)"
? authority(FSBOD_02, FSPOW_028, SFMainP045Record).
# => TRUE

# ── Where it stops ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Detection belongs to the attesters. Three who agree that there is no
# coalition complete the selection whether or not one exists, as the red-team
# collusion case shows for every record family. Nothing here concludes anything
# about a person.
? prisoner(SFMainP045Evidence).
# => FALSE
? false(SFMainP045Evidence).
# => FALSE
